    "q-182238": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182238",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are finite?\n\nI. $P(\\{R,e\\})$\n\nII. $P(\\{x\\in R∣\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0\\})$\n\nIII. $P(\\{(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z\\})$",
      "worked_solution": "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP(\\{R,e\\})=\\{∅,\\,\\{R\\},\\,\\{e\\},\\,\\{R,e\\}\\}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set II is infinite since the underlying set $\\{x\\in R∣\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0\\}$  is infinite.\n\n- Set III is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n\\{(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z\\}=\\{-1,1\\},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP(\\{(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z\\})=P(\\{-1,1\\})=\\{∅,\\,\\{-1\\},\\,\\{1\\},\\,\\{-1,1\\}\\}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
